From 63a37839963eece31c0daaa7edd322f85d5e6f74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephen Trotter <33046718+sjtrotter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:04:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] RDP: handle PKCS11 client certificates in WebKit

Certificate-based authentication in Azure AD challenges the embedded web
view for a TLS client certificate from certauth.<authority> and, when the
certificate lives on a smart card, for its PIN. WebKitGTK surfaces both as
"authenticate" signals that the AAD web view did not handle, so smart-card
users could not sign in through the embedded browser.

Handle WebKitAuthenticationRequest for client certificates and certificate
PINs. Certificates are discovered with p11-kit's "p11tool --list-certs --only-urls"
under a cancellable, time-bounded subprocess; the user chooses one in a
dialog and the selected certificate is loaded through GTlsCertificate off
the GTK thread with a bounded loading dialog so the main loop stays
responsive. A PIN prompt is accepted only for the certificate transaction
that presented the certificate, is answered once per challenge plus any
WebKit-initiated retry, and expires. Every challenge is bound to the verified https
authentication host recorded on the web view: only that authority and its
certauth. subdomain can receive a certificate, and the relationship is
defined in one place. The toplevel window is held with a reference across
the nested dialogs and released when the handler returns, so a window
destroyed under a nested loop is never dereferenced. The PIN is passed to
the request and never logged or retained.

Every stage is logged through the plugin's debug and warning channels
with a stable "smartcard-auth: <code>" reason code: the challenge (scheme,
host, port, proxy flag) and whether it was accepted, discovery start and
the token and certificate counts, the chosen index, load start, finish,
timeout or GError, PIN requests and why one was refused, and the source of
every cancellation. Only counts, reason codes, and the verified sign-in
host appear; PKCS #11 URIs, labels, serials, PINs, and callback URLs are
never logged, and loader error text is cut before any embedded URI.

p11tool exits non-zero for a token that holds no certificate (p11-kit's
System and Default Trust tokens are listed first and always do), so a
non-zero status with no URL output now counts the token as empty instead
of aborting discovery, and tokens whose model is p11-kit-trust are skipped
without a subprocess. Token-listing failures, cancellation, output limits,
URL output alongside a non-zero status, and a tool killed by a signal
remain fatal.

The sources are compiled only when WITH_RDP_AUTH_AAD is enabled, matching
the WebKit dependency they need.

Tested with FreeRDP 3.30.0. The series requires FreeRDP 3.16.0 or
newer: FreeRDP_GatewayAvdScope and FreeRDP_GatewayAvdAccessAadFormat
were added in that release, and every other API used is older.

This change was prepared with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic) and was
reviewed and tested by the author.
